      "text": "Real SDK shapes, one tiny Haiku turn (claude-haiku-4-5, low, full access, isolated yardd --engines real, --allow-spend) in /tmp/sa-real/proj: foreground Agent call. Events yardd logged: tool_started Agent {agent:general-purpose, detail:\"list files\"}; tool_started Ran {parent:<agent id>} \"ls -la\"; tool_completed for it; tool_completed for the Agent {ms:4070, output: the subagent report}; assistant_message \"done\"; turn_completed completed. An earlier raw SDK probe (a default background Agent) showed the tool_result is only a \"launched\" placeholder and task_notification arrives after the first turn result, which is why the notification ends the call. Not verified live: a background agent finishing in a later turn in the UI, and a real screenshot of it (only the scripted sidecar was drawn)."
    },
